"Annual Report 2025 | GUOCOLAND (MALAYSIA) BERHAD 21 (https://guocoland.com.my/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Guocoland-Annual-Report-2025.pdf)\nciteturn365search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11 months ago; Annual Report 2025 | GUOCOLAND (MALAYSIA) BERHAD 21 ... DC Residensi comprises 370 luxury serviced apartments, thoughtfully designed with a variety of layouts and complemented by premium amenities, offering residents refined urban living in one of the Kuala Lumpur’s most exclusive addresses.\nAnnual Report 2025 | GUOCOLAND (MALAYSIA) BERHAD 21\n\n# MANAGEMENT DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS cont’d\n\n## SEGMENTAL REVIEW OF OPERATIONS cont’d\n\n### Property Development cont’d\n\n#### Damansara City\n\nLocated in the prestigious and affluent neighbourhood of Damansara Heights, Kuala Lumpur, Damansara City is the area’s first transit-oriented integrated mixed development spanning 8.5 acres of freehold land. The development consists of two Grade A office towers, Menara Hong Leong and Menara Guoco, alongside two residential blocks, DC Residensi, the 5-star Sofitel Kuala Lumpur Damansara hotel and the five-storey DC Mall.\n\nMenara Guoco has been certified as a Green Building by the Green Building Index (GBI) and awarded Gold under the Leadership in Energy and Environmental Design (LEED) standard. DC Residensi comprises 370 luxury serviced apartments, thoughtfully designed with a variety of layouts and complemented by premium amenities, offering residents refined urban living in one of the Kuala Lumpur’s most exclusive addresses.\n\n### Property Investment\n\nOur property investment division continued to deliver sustainable growth in FY2025, driven by higher occupancy levels and stronger contributions across our diversified portfolio of investment assets. DC Mall achieved steady occupancy during the year, while Tower REIT benefitted from improved occupancy at Menara HLX.\n\n#### DC Mall\n\nAs an integral component of Damansara City, DC Mall is a five-storey community-centric mall focusing on healthcare and fitness concepts with a vibrant mix that includes dining, and retail services within its 172,826 square feet of net lettable area (NLA). In FY2025, DC Mall has achieved an overall occupancy rate of 82%. The tenant mix comprises Health & Wellness (28%), Retail & Services (9%), Food & Beverage (28%) and Supermarket (17%), reflecting a balanced portfolio that serves as a one-stop retail centre that caters to the needs of the surrounding community.\n\nThe DC Mall continues to draw increased foot traffic with its diverse lineup of tenants. The DC Food Bazaar remains a popular lunch destination, complemented by established names such as Jaya Grocer, Watsons, Health Lane, MyNEWS, MR DIY and CU Mart.\n\nIn the current financial year, several new tenants were secured, including Anytime Fitness, The Grappling Centre and Champur, which collectively took up 9,935 square feet, or approximately 5.7% of the lettable area. An expansion by an existing tenant, Good Juji, added another 3,309 square feet, bringing its total occupied area to 9,532 square feet. In addition, our anchor tenant, Jaya Grocer, remains a key draw, while KL Fertility is set to expand its premises to 15,816 square feet, thereby strengthening the mall’s healthcare offering.\n\nTo enhance its appeal further, DC Mall is exploring opportunities to attract more healthcare providers and fitness operators, diversifying its tenant base to meet the growing needs of the community. These efforts are expected to reinforce DC Mall’s positioning as a well-rounded one-stop retail centre in Damansara Heights.\n\n<visual_element id=\"e1\">\nPhoto of DC Mall building exterior, a tall blue-glass tower viewed from below against the sky, with “DC MALL” signage on the lower facade and a gold caption bar above the image labeled “DC Mall”.\n</visual_element>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGuocoLand Malaysia (https://guocoland.com.my/contact/)\nciteturn365s